{
  "title": "iOS local search using the shared search-ranking vectors",
  "description": "Search relevance ranking is implemented server-side as a \
pure scoring function in ramekin-core/src/search.rs, with ranking vectors at \
ramekin-core/tests/fixtures/search_ranking/cases.json. Those vectors do not \
cover query parsing or result membership. The complete parity requirements are \
recorded in doc/local-recipe-search-and-sync.md. Web stays server-side because \
it has no offline requirement or local recipe corpus.\n\
\n\
Scope when unblocked:\n\
- Pin the complete PostgreSQL `unaccent.rules` behavior as a versioned shared \
asset, verify every mapping against `f_unaccent` in an API test, and fail sync \
when iOS does not support the server's normalization-contract version.\n\
- Implement Swift query parsing, exact normalization, AND matching across the \
five bare-text fields, explicit `tag:`, and cached photo-presence and \
created-date filters. Implement relevance scoring plus updated-date, rating, \
and created-date ordering with server-identical tie-breaks.\n\
- Implement `tag:` as whole-value PostgreSQL `CITEXT` parity: case-insensitive \
but accent-sensitive equality, separate from the bare-text unaccent substring \
normalizer. Add server-backed vectors proving case and accent behavior.\n\
- Keep text queries containing `source:`, `photo_size:`, `photo_dim:`, or \
title/random ordering on the server. `SyncRecipe` lacks the source and \
detailed photo metadata, while iOS title collation differs from PostgreSQL. \
Add routing tests for every unsupported combination.\n\
- Extend `SyncRecipe` and the CoreData cache with the server-produced \
ingredient JSONB match text, preserving its distinction from the flattened \
structured ingredient inputs used by the scorer.\n\
- Add shared end-to-end match/filter vectors (raw query + recipe documents in, \
matched and ordered IDs out) alongside the existing ranking vectors. Consume \
both suites from server tests and XCTest, covering quotes, filters, accents, \
ligatures, multi-token AND semantics, and JSON-key-only ingredient matches.\n\
- Wire every shared vector path into iOS CI so a contract edit cannot merge \
without running the Swift side.\n\
\n\
Per doc/client-logic-sharing.md this is the duplicate-and-pin pattern; do NOT \
reach for WASM/UniFFI for a ~100-line scorer.",
  "status": "open",
